{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794429850","published":"2026-11-11T20:44:31Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:42.722905188Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-105081","CVE-2026-106566","CVE-2026-106570","CVE-2026-116140","CVE-2026-55628"],"summary":"Fix of 20 CVEs","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: delegate policy bypass through shell operators\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116140.patch: split shell operators, backticks\n       and escapes into separate tokens in StringToArgv() in magick/string.c,\n       and check every executable token against the delegate policy in\n       ExternalDelegateCommand() in magick/delegate.c\n     - CVE-2026-116140\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: path policy bypass through a dangling symbolic link\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-105081.patch: deny a path that is a symbolic\n       link which does not resolve in IsRightsAuthorized() in magick/policy.c\n     - CVE-2026-105081\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: missing path policy checks in -concatenate\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-55628.patch: check the read and write path\n       policy for the inputs and the output in ConcatenateImages() in\n       wand/convert.c\n     - CVE-2026-55628\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: delegate input symbolic link overwritten by shredding\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106566.patch: do not use a symbolic link for\n       the delegate input when MAGICK_SHRED_PASSES or the shred policy is set\n       in AcquireUniqueSymbolicLink() in magick/utility.c\n     - CVE-2026-106566\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: connection exhaustion of the distributed pixel cache\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106570.patch: add a 5 second receive deadline\n       to the command and key reads of the server in\n       magick/distribute-cache.c\n     - CVE-2026-106570","affected":[{"package":{"name":"imagemagick","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8:6.8.9.9-7ubuntu5.17+tuxcare.els69"}]}],"data